{
  // The game running with no session named, which is the one state #406's notice is for: zones B
  // and C and band D's fuel page should read "… · Go into a session" while the rest of the face
  // draws normally. `inSession()` is GameRunning and a named session type, so stopping the
  // emulator does not reach it -- that makes GameRunning false and SimHub switches to the idle
  // screen of #113 instead. The emulator has to keep running and say nothing about the session.
  //
  // What blanks it: SimHub's iRacing reader takes GameData.SessionTypeName from the session whose
  // SessionNum matches the telemetry's SessionNum and returns that session's SessionType verbatim
  // (GD_SessionTypeName in the decompiled ICarsReader 9.12.6; it falls back to
  // WeekendInfo.EventType only when no session matches). So the one field to blank is that
  // session's SessionType, and blanking it reaches SimHub as an empty name rather than as the
  // previous one, because the emulator re-renders the whole session string and bumps
  // sessionInfoUpdate whenever it changes. An empty scalar is already in this document --
  // `SessionSubType:` has always been empty and SimHub parses it -- so the blank costs nothing at
  // the parser.
  //
  // SessionNum stays 2, which is deliberate: GD_TotalLaps indexes Sessions[SessionNum] directly,
  // so pointing the telemetry at a session that is not in the list would throw inside SimHub
  // rather than draw a notice. SessionName stays RACE because nothing reads it.
  //
  // Held still, like the capture scenarios, since the notice is the whole of what it is here to
  // show: it extends green, so the flag is green from the first tick and the limiter is off.
  "extends": "green.json",
  "name": "Game running, no session named",
  "yaml": {
    "RaceSessionType": ""
  }
}
